# ROOT files published by CERN, used to measure the specification's coverage.
# NOT part of data/: these are not our fixtures and are not committed.
#   https://root.cern/files/  and  https://root.cern/files/rootbench/
# Fetch with tools/fetch_cern.py; gen/cern/README.md says why each file is here.
#
# Unlike gen/foreign/, every file here was written by ROOT itself, so a failure
# is evidence about the format rather than a lead to be traced to a writer.
#
# Columns: sha256, bytes, the ROOT version in the file header, tier, remote path
# relative to https://root.cern/files/.
#
# Tier "core" is 24 files and 5.5 MB: the version sweep, the divergent classes and
# the containers that find things. Tier "physics" is 27 MB of real production
# trees, useful as a regression corpus and nothing else. The multi-gigabyte files
# are in LARGE.toml and are read by range request, never downloaded.
